  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 1. Why is a voltmeter always connected in parallel with the circuit?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: Voltmeter is used to measure the potential difference across two
    points. Since the objects in parallel have the same potential, a voltmeter should
    always be connected in parallel.
  options:
  - Because the objects in parallel have the same potential difference.
  - Because the objects in parallel have the same current.
  - Because the objects in series have the same potential difference.
  - Because the objects in series have the same resistance.
  correctOptionIndex: 0
